          <td data-label="Output">Decision note</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="saflow">The path of a recording from microphone to listener</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Stage</th>
          <th>What happens</th>
          <th>Skill</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Capture</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Record in a quiet space with a steady distance from the microphone</td>
          <td data-label="Skill">Room control and mic technique</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Edit</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Remove mistakes, breaths and long gaps</td>
          <td data-label="Skill">Careful listening</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Clean</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Reduce hum and background noise gently</td>
          <td data-label="Skill">Restraint, since heavy cleaning damages voices</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Balance</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Set levels so speech and music sit well together</td>
          <td data-label="Skill">Level judgement</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Master</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Match loudness to platform norms</td>
          <td data-label="Skill">Reference listening</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Stage"><strong>Deliver</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What happens">Export in the required format and name files clearly</td>
          <td data-label="Skill">File discipline</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Practise each stage on the same short clip so you hear how every choice changes the result.
  </p>
  <p>
    Keep the original recording untouched and work on copies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="saroom">Fixing a poor room before buying gear</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Problem</th>
          <th>Cheap fix</th>
          <th>Check</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Problem"><strong>Echo</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Cheap fix">Record near soft furnishings such as curtains and a mattress</td>
          <td data-label="Check">Clap and listen for ring</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Problem"><strong>Outside noise</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Cheap fix">Record at quieter hours and close windows</td>
          <td data-label="Check">Listen on headphones</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Problem"><strong>Fan or air conditioner hum</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Cheap fix">Switch off while recording</td>
          <td data-label="Check">Check the silence between words</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Problem"><strong>Mouth noise and pops</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Cheap fix">Keep a hand width from the microphone and angle it slightly</td>
          <td data-label="Check">Listen for hard letters</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    A treated room with a basic microphone usually beats an expensive microphone in an echoing room.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sagig">Live sound basics to learn with a mentor</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
